    skos:scopeNote "(TSI INF 4.2.7.1.2(2)) Applicable if the maximum permitted speed of the running track is more than 200km/h and the structures within the section of line are all compatible with the High Speed Load Model (HSLM); information regarding the procedure to be used to perform the dynamic compatibility check shall be provided as well."@en .

era:hotAxleBoxDetectorDirection a owl:FunctionalProperty,
        owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Direction of measurement of trackside HABD"@en ;
    era:XMLName "IHS_HABDDirection" ;
    era:applicable "Y/N" ;
    era:dependencyNote "Mandatory if the HABD is not TSI compliant (the value of parameter 1.1.1.1.7.5 (Trackside HABD TSI compliant) is 'False')"@en ;
    era:inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/hot-axle-box-detector-direction/HotAxleBoxDetectorDirections> ;
    era:legalDeadline "16 January 2020"@en ;
    era:rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.7.9" ;
    era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/HotAxleBoxDetectorDirection>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/HotAxleBoxDetectorDirectionApplicability>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/HotAxleBoxDetectorDirectionCountryApplicability>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/HotAxleBoxDetectorDirectionSKOS> ;
    era:usedInRCCCalculations true ;
    dcterms:created "2022-07-08"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-01-08"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-20"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Direction of measurement of trackside HABD, specific for the French Italian and Swedish networks."@en ;
    rdfs:domain era:HABD ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy era: ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf era:healthSafetyAndEnvironmentObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:changeNote "This property was previously a datatype property with domain Track and range string. As its values are a list of three predefined values, it is now a SKOS."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Specific for the French Italian and Swedish networks.
Applicable if trackside HABD is not TSI compliant, direction of measurement of trackside hot axle box detector.
If the direction of measurement is:
-	the same as the direction defined by the start and end of the SoL: (N)
-	the opposite to the direction defined by the start and end of the SoL: (O)
-	both directions: (B)"""@en .

