era:Certificate a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Certificate"@en ;
    dcterms:created "2022-06-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2022-06-15"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-10-24"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-04-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2016/797/2020-05-28>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2016/798/2020-10-23> ;
    rdfs:comment "Base class for those Certificates in the ERADIS register, which allow a IOD/SD described process."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy era: ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/vpa#Permission> ;
    owl:deprecated false ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """In the context of the ERA vocabulary, a Certificate (`vpa:Permission`) can be:
- Safety Certificate (`vpa:grantedBy` NSA, `vpa:requestedBy` RailwayUndertaking), permitting 'access to the railway infrastructure' (SD Art. 10).
- Safety Authorisation (`vpa:grantedBy` NSA, `vpa:requestedBy` InfrastructureManager), permitting 'to manage and operate a rail infrastructure' (SD Art.12)
- Licence for the performance of rail transport services within the Union and the European Economic Area
- ECM Certificates, permitting to act as an ECM
- ...

Note: The `Interoperability documents` in ERADIS must use other Classes:
- EC DoV, EC DoC, EC DoSoU are issued by Applicants (use `era:ECDeclaration`);
- CLD's are issued by NoBo's (use `era:CLD`)"""@en .

